cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it."
title: "PostQuantumSafe IoT Cybersecurity (TIPPSS SafeGuard-PQ): An Agentic Testing Framework for Post-Quantum Safety of IoT and Edge Environments"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Manjunath"
    given-names: "Pavan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2694-8807"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-24"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pavangemmanjunath-cell/PostQuantumSafe_IoT_Cybersecurity"
url: "https://github.com/pavangemmanjunath-cell/PostQuantumSafe_IoT_Cybersecurity"
license: "Apache-2.0"
abstract: >-
  Open-source research prototype of an agentic testing framework that checks whether an IoT and edge-device
  environment is safe against post-quantum (quantum computer) attacks. Fourteen deterministic agents inventory the
  cryptographic primitives of each device, identify post-quantum exposure against NIST FIPS 203, 204 and 205, detect
  identity, privacy, AI-prompt and network risks, map every finding to the IEEE 2933-2024 TIPPSS pillars (trust,
  identity, privacy, protection, safety, security), explain every result with evidence, exact score attributions and
  counterfactuals, and plan countermeasures under budget and downtime limits with a quantum-inspired optimiser (QIRO).
  Includes a FastAPI backend, a React and three.js interface with an IoT fleet simulator, post-quantum attack
  injection and a Q-Day what-if, and PDF reports that state whether the environment is safe. Contributions are welcome.
keywords:
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - quantum-safe
  - Internet of Things
  - IoT security
  - edge devices
  - cybersecurity
  - agentic testing
  - multi-agent systems
  - explainable AI
  - TIPPSS
  - IEEE 2933
  - healthcare security
  - research software
